&lt;p&gt;Developing Tolerix with an AI agent allowed rapid iteration across mathematically demanding components: implementing analytical Bézier curve derivative extrema, verifying 2D affine transform matrix multiplication, establishing DOM sanitization rules against SVG-based exploits, and engineering zero-cloud IndexedDB workflows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  My First User
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I showed Tolerix to Uncle, a maker who runs a custom wooden signage and acrylic badge side business out of his workshop using an 80W CO2 laser.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;He tested the app by pasting an actual customer email request ("Please cut 25 frosted acrylic badges, 75 x 45 mm, with rounded corners and our logo engraved") along with the customer's uploaded SVG file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix immediately caught two problems:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The SVG geometry was drawn at 60 x 36 mm instead of the requested 75 x 45 mm (a scaling error from the customer's design software).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The outer perimeter was split into two unjoined path segments rather than a single continuous closed contour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;He said: "Catching that scale error before cutting saved me an entire 12 x 24 inch acrylic sheet ($18) and thirty minutes of re-cutting. Having this run right on my shop laptop without logging into a cloud service makes it a no-brainer."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Prize Categories
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Best Use of Gemma
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix enters the &lt;strong&gt;Best Use of Gemma&lt;/strong&gt; category. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It directly integrates Google's open-weight Gemma models (&lt;code&gt;gemma-4-E2B-it-litert-lm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;gemma-4-E4B-it-litert-lm&lt;/code&gt;) executing on device via the LiteRT-LM WebGPU runtime:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;On-Device Inference:&lt;/strong&gt; Downloads verified weights into the browser Cache Storage API (&lt;code&gt;tolerix-models-v1&lt;/code&gt;) with full byte-level integrity verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Structured Parsing:&lt;/strong&gt; Gemma parses ambiguous natural language instructions into structured manufacturing specifications (quantity, bounding box dimensions, physical units, material type, thickness, and cutting/engraving operations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Graceful Degradation:&lt;/strong&gt; Users can switch between Gemma 2B (for lightweight laptop GPUs) and Gemma 4B (for high-precision extraction), with deterministic heuristics serving as a fallback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Best Use of Render
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tolerix is deployed in Render&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Helpdesk: "Jordan hit Record in yesterday's standup and the chat still has no link. Sam says the Record button is greyed out with a lock. Priya's channel town-hall recording isn't under Files either, and Marcus wants us to reinstall Teams for everyone so recordings 'just work' again. Can you force the recording to upload?"&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Don't reinstall Teams yet. &lt;strong&gt;"Teams meeting recording not working" is usually one broken layer in a documented policy-and-storage chain&lt;/strong&gt;, not a missing Force Upload button: &lt;strong&gt;the user can't start recording (license, role, meeting options, or meeting/calling policy)&lt;/strong&gt; → &lt;strong&gt;the recording finished but landed somewhere other than this chat (organizer OneDrive Recordings, channel SharePoint, or a co-organizer fallback)&lt;/strong&gt; → &lt;strong&gt;the link is delayed, scrolled out of a busy chat, or expired into recycle&lt;/strong&gt; → &lt;strong&gt;upload failed to async media storage and the 21-day download window is ticking&lt;/strong&gt;. Microsoft's meeting-recording troubleshooting, storage/permissions, cloud-recording policy, and expiration articles are the sources for that chain — not a tip that says "wipe the client."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the real problem is &lt;strong&gt;SharePoint/OneDrive external sharing or guest access to a site&lt;/strong&gt; (not the Record button), start with &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/sharepoint-external-sharing-not-working-a-read-first-org-site-domain-and-entra-b2b-triage-iae"&gt;SharePoint External Sharing Not Working&lt;/a&gt;. If the &lt;strong&gt;file was deleted or expired into recycle&lt;/strong&gt;, use &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/restore-a-deleted-sharepoint-site-onedrive-or-file-in-microsoft-365-step-by-step-with-the-time-8lf"&gt;Restore a Deleted SharePoint Site, OneDrive, or File&lt;/a&gt;. If OneDrive &lt;strong&gt;sync client&lt;/strong&gt; is stuck (Processing changes) so the user can't open a recording they already own, start with &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/onedrive-sync-stuck-processing-changes-a-read-first-client-files-on-demand-and-sync-engine-triage-22id"&gt;OneDrive Sync Stuck Processing Changes&lt;/a&gt; — not this post. This post covers &lt;strong&gt;"Record is missing / greyed out, or the meeting recorded but nobody can find the MP4 — and you need a read-first path before rebuild."&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Split the ticket first.&lt;/strong&gt; Missing / locked &lt;strong&gt;Record&lt;/strong&gt; button ≠ recording finished but &lt;strong&gt;not in chat&lt;/strong&gt; ≠ recording &lt;strong&gt;expired&lt;/strong&gt;. Those are different layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Both organizer and recorder need recording permission.&lt;/strong&gt; Guests and federated/external users cannot start convenience recording in your tenant. Attendees may be blocked by role or by Meeting options → Recording &amp;amp; transcription.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Storage is not "inside Teams."&lt;/strong&gt; Non-channel meetings → organizer's &lt;strong&gt;OneDrive &amp;gt; My files &amp;gt; Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; (even if someone else hit Record). Channel meetings → team &lt;strong&gt;SharePoint &amp;gt; Documents &amp;gt; Recordings&lt;/strong&gt;. 1:1 / group calls → the person who selected Record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Find before you rebuild.&lt;/strong&gt; Scroll the chat (high-volume chat can hide the link), open Meeting recap / Recordings &amp;amp; transcripts, open the Recordings folder, then run admin &lt;strong&gt;Missing Recording Diagnostic&lt;/strong&gt; (join URL + date; telemetry ~&lt;strong&gt;30 days&lt;/strong&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Expiration is policy, not "Teams ate it."&lt;/strong&gt; Default automatic expiration is often &lt;strong&gt;120 days&lt;/strong&gt; (admin-controlled). Expired files move to the &lt;strong&gt;recycle bin&lt;/strong&gt; of that OneDrive/SharePoint location — restore there, don't reinstall the app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Quota / no OneDrive → async storage.&lt;/strong&gt; If upload fails (no OneDrive / full quota), Microsoft temporarily holds the recording for download for &lt;strong&gt;21 days&lt;/strong&gt;, then deletes it. Download immediately when chat offers it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Where in the chain did it break?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Step&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What should be true&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Typical symptom when it breaks&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1. Symptom captured&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Record missing vs lock vs recorded/no link vs expired banner&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;"Teams recording broken" with no string&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;2. Meeting type&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Meeting vs 1:1 call vs channel vs shared-mailbox organizer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Troubleshooting meeting policy on a call&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;3. Who can press Record&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;License + role + meeting options&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Attendee / guest / Copilot-off organizer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;4. Tenant policy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Meeting policy AllowCloudRecording (or calling policy for calls)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Whole cohort can't record after policy change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5. Storage location&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Correct OD Recordings or SP Recordings folder&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hunting only in the wrong person's OneDrive&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;6. Find + diagnostics&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Chat / Recap / folder / Missing Recording Diagnostic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Rebuild Teams before looking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;7. Expiration / recycle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Not expired; recycle still holds file&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;"Unavailable" banner treated as never recorded&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;8. Quota / async&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OneDrive exists; space free; or 21-day download used&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Waiting for auto-retry that never comes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 1: Capture the exact symptom (read-only)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Write five facts on the ticket before Reset Teams / Clear cache / "reinstall for the floor":&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Fact&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Why it matters&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exact UI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Record missing; lock icon + tooltip; Record worked but no chat link; Recap says unavailable/expired; upload-failed + Download&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meeting type&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Scheduled/Meet now; channel meeting; 1:1 or group call; webinar/town hall; shared-mailbox organizer&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who hit Record&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Organizer, co-organizer, presenter, or "nobody could"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Meeting end time + how long they waited for processing&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;One user / one meeting / whole department after a policy change&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then compare:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hover any &lt;strong&gt;lock&lt;/strong&gt; on Record — Microsoft's troubleshooting doc: the tooltip often states why the control is unavailable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open &lt;strong&gt;Meeting options → Recording &amp;amp; transcription&lt;/strong&gt; (organizer) — who is allowed to record/transcribe?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check &lt;strong&gt;Microsoft 365 Service Health&lt;/strong&gt; for Teams / OneDrive / SharePoint before you blame the client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm the user is signed in as the &lt;strong&gt;expected work account&lt;/strong&gt; (not a personal/guest context).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Pattern&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Likely layer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Record missing for everyone in a policy group&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Meeting / calling policy (Step 4)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lock for one attendee; organizer can record&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Role / meeting options (Step 3)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Guest or federated user can't record&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Expected — convenience recording (Step 3)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recording finished; no chat link; busy chat&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Find / scroll (Step 6)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Channel meeting; nothing under chat Files&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;SharePoint Recordings folder (Step 5)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;"Unavailable" / expired on Recap&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Expiration / recycle (Step 7)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Upload failed + Download offered&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Async media / quota (Step 8)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1:1 call Record missing; meetings OK&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Calling policy, not meeting policy (Step 2/4)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 2: Confirm meeting vs call vs channel (read-only)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Microsoft's troubleshooting guidance starts here because &lt;strong&gt;controls and policies differ by workload&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Kind&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Recording policy surface&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Where the file lands (typical)&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Scheduled / Meet now (non-channel)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams &lt;strong&gt;meeting&lt;/strong&gt; policy (&lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Organizer&lt;/strong&gt; OneDrive &lt;code&gt;Recordings&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Channel meeting&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Same meeting policy; channel SharePoint permissions&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Team site &lt;strong&gt;Documents / Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; (or View only folder if download blocked)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1:1 or group &lt;strong&gt;call&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Teams &lt;strong&gt;calling&lt;/strong&gt; policy (&lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecordingForCalls&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OneDrive of the user who selected &lt;strong&gt;Record&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Webinar / town hall&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Events&lt;/strong&gt; policy recording toggles&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OneDrive / VOD paths — treat as events, not a standup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared mailbox organizers (sidebar):&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft: for meetings scheduled with a shared mailbox, the shared mailbox is the organizer. If that account has no OneDrive (common), the recording uploads to a &lt;strong&gt;co-organizer&lt;/strong&gt; or the &lt;strong&gt;recording initiator&lt;/strong&gt; OneDrive instead. Shared mailboxes without a Teams license follow the &lt;strong&gt;Global&lt;/strong&gt; meeting policy — if Global &lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/code&gt; is false, users can't record those meetings. Assign a Teams license before a custom meeting policy on that identity. For shared-mailbox &lt;em&gt;Outlook visibility&lt;/em&gt; tickets, use &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/shared-mailbox-not-showing-in-outlook-a-read-first-full-access-automapping-and-client-triage-57e0"&gt;Shared Mailbox Not Showing in Outlook&lt;/a&gt; — different problem.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight powershell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Read-only: meeting policy assignment + cloud recording flag (Teams PowerShell)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Connect-MicrosoftTeams   # interactive admin session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;

&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Get-CsOnlineUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'jordan@contoso.com'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Select-Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UserPrincipalName&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;TeamsMeetingPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;TeamsCallingPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;

&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Get-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Global&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Select-Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
                &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ChannelRecordingDownload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ExplicitRecordingConsent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;

&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# If the user has a custom meeting policy, read that Identity too:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Get-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy -Identity 'Contoso-Standard' |&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;#   Select-Object Identity, AllowCloudRecording, NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;






&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 3: License, role, and meeting options (read-only)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before you flip tenant policy:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;License.&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft Support: both the &lt;strong&gt;meeting organizer&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;person who records&lt;/strong&gt; need a qualifying Microsoft 365 / Office 365 license that includes Teams cloud recording (for example Enterprise E1/E3/E5/F3, Education A1/A3/A5, or Microsoft 365 Business SKUs listed in Support). Confirm the affected accounts still have Teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Role in the meeting.&lt;/strong&gt; Attendees may be blocked. Organizer can promote to &lt;strong&gt;presenter&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong&gt;co-organizer&lt;/strong&gt; when policy allows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Meeting options.&lt;/strong&gt; Organizer: Meeting options → &lt;strong&gt;Recording &amp;amp; transcription&lt;/strong&gt; → who can record and transcribe. Teams Premium organizers get finer controls — read what is set before changing Global policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Guests / federated / anonymous.&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft: guests can't initiate convenience recordings; users in trusted organizations can't initiate convenience recordings when they join &lt;em&gt;your&lt;/em&gt; meetings (compliance recording is a different product). Have an internal organizer/presenter start Record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Copilot-off note.&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft Learn: when organizers turn off Microsoft Copilot in Teams meetings/events, &lt;strong&gt;recording and transcription are also turned off&lt;/strong&gt;. If "Copilot off" was the change request yesterday, check that before chasing &lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Admin diagnostic (account):&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft 365 admin center → run &lt;strong&gt;Meeting Recording Support Diagnostic&lt;/strong&gt; / Teams Meeting Recording Test for the user who can't press Record (license + meeting policy prerequisites). Not available in all sovereign clouds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Leave/rejoin and Teams &lt;strong&gt;web&lt;/strong&gt; client are Microsoft's light client workarounds after policy/role look correct — still not "reinstall the fleet."&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 4: Read the meeting (or calling) policy (read-only → careful change)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Teams admin center:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Meetings → Meeting policies&lt;/strong&gt; → open the policy assigned to the organizer (and the recorder).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm &lt;strong&gt;Meeting recording&lt;/strong&gt; (cloud recording) is &lt;strong&gt;On&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note &lt;strong&gt;Recordings and transcriptions automatically expire&lt;/strong&gt; / default expiration days (Step 7).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For calls: &lt;strong&gt;Voice → Calling policies&lt;/strong&gt; → cloud recording for calls / &lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecordingForCalls&lt;/code&gt; — only if Step 2 said this was a call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PowerShell (read first; change only after the ticket names the policy):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight powershell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# Read-only examples — do not Set- until the read agrees on the layer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Get-CsTeamsMeetingPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Select-Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;NewMeetingRecordingExpirationDays&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
                &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ChannelRecordingDownload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Format-Table&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-AutoSize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;

&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Get-CsTeamsCallingPolicy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;-Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Global&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;Select-Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Identity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AllowCloudRecordingForCalls&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Both&lt;/strong&gt; organizer and recorder need recording enabled on the policies that apply to them. Fixing only the person who clicked Record while the organizer's policy blocks cloud recording still fails.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 5: Map storage before you search the wrong Drive (read-only)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Microsoft's storage model (convenience recording):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Meeting shape&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Who selected Record&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Where the file goes&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Non-channel meeting / event&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Anyone allowed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Organizer's&lt;/strong&gt; OneDrive &lt;code&gt;Recordings&lt;/code&gt; (organizer need not attend)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Non-channel; organizer has &lt;strong&gt;no&lt;/strong&gt; OneDrive&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Co-organizer OneDrive in meeting-options order → else initiator → else &lt;strong&gt;async&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Channel meeting&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Channel member&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Team SharePoint library &lt;strong&gt;Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; folder&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;1:1 / group call&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Caller or callee&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;That person's&lt;/strong&gt; OneDrive&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Shared mailbox organizer, no OD&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Co-organizer / initiator OneDrive (see Step 2)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Permissions (short form Microsoft documents):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-channel: invitees in the org typically get a shared link; &lt;strong&gt;external/guest&lt;/strong&gt; viewers need an explicit share from the owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Channel: permissions follow the channel / SharePoint membership (and &lt;code&gt;ChannelRecordingDownload&lt;/code&gt; Allow vs Block / View only folder).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large meetings (&lt;strong&gt;&amp;gt;250&lt;/strong&gt; participants): some people may &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; get automatic file permissions — ask the owner to add them to the share list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OneDrive adjacency:&lt;/strong&gt; if the organizer's Known Folder Move / silent sign-in is broken, that is not why Record is missing — but it can confuse "I don't see Recordings under Desktop." Use &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/intune-onedrive-known-folder-move-not-working-a-read-first-silent-sign-in-and-policy-triage-551i"&gt;Intune OneDrive Known Folder Move Not Working&lt;/a&gt; only for KFM. Recording files still live under the &lt;strong&gt;cloud&lt;/strong&gt; Recordings folder even when Desktop redirect is unhappy.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 6: Find the recording (read-only → diagnostic)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Work top-down:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Meeting chat:&lt;/strong&gt; Microsoft documents a high-volume chat issue where the recording link doesn't appear. &lt;strong&gt;Scroll to top, then back to bottom&lt;/strong&gt; to refresh the chat service event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Meeting recap / Recordings &amp;amp; transcripts&lt;/strong&gt; tab on the calendar item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Manual path&lt;/strong&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-channel: &lt;code&gt;onedrive.com&lt;/code&gt; → &lt;strong&gt;My files → Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; (organizer — or co-organizer/initiator per Step 5).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Channel: Teams channel → &lt;strong&gt;Files → Recordings → Open in SharePoint&lt;/strong&gt;, or SharePoint &lt;code&gt;Documents/&amp;lt;Channel&amp;gt;/Recordings&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Missing Recording Diagnostic&lt;/strong&gt; (admin): Microsoft 365 admin center → Help → diagnose &lt;strong&gt;Missing Recording&lt;/strong&gt; / Meeting Recording Missing. Enter the &lt;strong&gt;meeting join URL&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;meeting date&lt;/strong&gt;. Confirms whether processing/upload finished and which OD/SP location was used. Microsoft: recording telemetry is retained about &lt;strong&gt;30 days&lt;/strong&gt; — older meetings need the manual folder search / recycle path instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If search finds nothing but the file exists in Recordings, that is a &lt;strong&gt;search&lt;/strong&gt; ticket — &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/sharepoint-search-not-working-a-read-first-visibility-permission-and-reindex-triage-4162"&gt;SharePoint Search Not Working&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 7: Expiration, recycle, and Purview (read-only → restore)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Signal&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Prefer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Recap banner: recording unavailable / check with organizer whether still uploading, &lt;strong&gt;expired&lt;/strong&gt;, or deleted&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Treat as expiration or delete — not "never recorded"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Admin &lt;strong&gt;Meetings automatically expire&lt;/strong&gt; / Recordings and transcriptions automatically expire &lt;strong&gt;On&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Default expiration often &lt;strong&gt;120 days&lt;/strong&gt; (policy). Changes apply to &lt;strong&gt;new&lt;/strong&gt; recordings; admins can't bulk-edit old expiration in the policy&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Owner can still edit the file&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Organizer/co-organizer can change or remove expiration on the player page when they have edit rights&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;File gone from Recordings&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OneDrive or SharePoint &lt;strong&gt;recycle bin&lt;/strong&gt; for that location — restore with &lt;a href="https://dev.to/adminpackstudio/restore-a-deleted-sharepoint-site-onedrive-or-file-in-microsoft-365-step-by-step-with-the-time-8lf"&gt;DEVTO_24&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Purview retention on OD/SP&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Retention &lt;strong&gt;takes precedence&lt;/strong&gt; over Teams expiration delete until retention completes (Microsoft compliance guidance)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Microsoft: after expiration the file moves to recycle (often within about a day, rarely longer); owner gets email; recovering from recycle clears automatic re-expiration for that copy. Watching the recording does &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; extend expiration.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 8: Quota, no OneDrive, and async media storage (read-only → download)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If chat shows &lt;strong&gt;upload failed&lt;/strong&gt; / offers &lt;strong&gt;Download&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Download the MP4 &lt;strong&gt;immediately&lt;/strong&gt; — Microsoft: when organizer, co-organizers, and initiator lack OneDrive (or quota is full), the recording goes to &lt;strong&gt;async media storage&lt;/strong&gt;. There is &lt;strong&gt;no automatic retry&lt;/strong&gt; to OneDrive/SharePoint. If not downloaded within &lt;strong&gt;21 days&lt;/strong&gt;, it is deleted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free OneDrive/SharePoint quota or license OneDrive, then re-upload manually if needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning hint from Microsoft: roughly &lt;strong&gt;~400 MB per hour&lt;/strong&gt; of recording — capacity planning matters for heavy meeting cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;IP-restricted SharePoint and channel recording upload have documented limitations; Microsoft recommends Conditional Access patterns rather than IP allow lists for channel recording scenarios — don't "fix" that with a Teams reinstall.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 9: Change one thing (only after the read)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After Steps 1–8 agree on the layer:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fix &lt;strong&gt;role / meeting options&lt;/strong&gt; for this meeting &lt;strong&gt;or&lt;/strong&gt; assign/correct &lt;strong&gt;meeting policy&lt;/strong&gt; for the organizer — one change.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retest Record in a &lt;strong&gt;short test meeting&lt;/strong&gt; (not the executive all-hands).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If the issue was find/expire: open the correct &lt;strong&gt;Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; folder or &lt;strong&gt;restore from recycle&lt;/strong&gt; — don't flip &lt;code&gt;AllowCloudRecording&lt;/code&gt; "to be safe."
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If async download was offered: save the file first, then fix quota/license.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Only then try leave/rejoin or web client; client reinstall last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  When a change is justified
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Finding&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Prefer&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Avoid&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
