&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why is the Teams Record button missing or locked?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
In order: wrong workload (&lt;strong&gt;call&lt;/strong&gt; vs &lt;strong&gt;meeting&lt;/strong&gt;), &lt;strong&gt;role&lt;/strong&gt; (attendee), &lt;strong&gt;meeting options&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;license&lt;/strong&gt;, organizer &lt;strong&gt;Copilot/recording&lt;/strong&gt; off, or meeting/calling &lt;strong&gt;policy&lt;/strong&gt; with cloud recording disabled. Hover the lock for the tooltip; run the Meeting Recording Support Diagnostic for the user.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where does a Teams meeting recording go?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Non-channel → organizer's OneDrive &lt;strong&gt;Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; (even if a presenter started recording). Channel → that team's SharePoint &lt;strong&gt;Recordings&lt;/strong&gt; folder. 1:1/group call → OneDrive of whoever selected Record. Shared mailbox organizers without OneDrive fall through to co-organizer/initiator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recording finished but nothing in chat — did it fail?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Not always. Scroll the chat, check Recap / Recordings &amp;amp; transcripts, then the Recordings folder. Admins can run &lt;strong&gt;Missing Recording Diagnostic&lt;/strong&gt; with join URL + date (best within ~30 days of telemetry). High-volume chats can hide the link until refreshed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How long until recordings disappear?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
If automatic expiration is on, Microsoft's default is often &lt;strong&gt;120 days&lt;/strong&gt; (admin sets the value). Expired files go to the OneDrive/SharePoint recycle bin for that location. Organizers with edit rights can change or remove expiration on the player for recordings they control. Purview retention can keep files longer than Teams expiration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Can guests record our Teams meetings?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Not with convenience cloud recording. Guests and federated users joining your meetings can't start that recording. An internal organizer/presenter records; share the file if externals need playback (explicit share — guests don't automatically get non-channel recording links).&lt;/p&gt;




